<title>USA: Unocal says Wilmington unit shut Saturday.</title>
<headline>Unocal says Wilmington unit shut Saturday.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unocal Corp said on Wednesday that it shut on Saturday a hydrocracking unit at its 130,000 barrel-per-day refinery near Los Angeles, Calif.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman declined to say when the plant would try to restart the unit, nor would she specify the cause of the unplanned shutdown.</p>
<p>The problem was not caused by a fire or explosion, she said. Gasoline output at the refinery is normally 75,000 bpd.</p>
<p>The plant is one of three which is expected to be sold to Tosco Corp sometime in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Los Angeles Bureau, +1 213 380 2014</p>
</text>
